  "releaseNotes": "Adds the ability to set the sensor reporting interval on Tapo hub child sensors (T100, T110, T310, T315, S200B, and similar). ChildReportModeModule.ReportInterval was previously read-only. KasaDevice.SetChildReportIntervalAsync (childDeviceId, seconds) and ChildReportModeModule.SetIntervalAsync (seconds) now issue set_device_info with a report_interval parameter over the existing control_child envelope, then refresh parent state. The value and its persistence were confirmed against a live T100 and S200B by writing a new interval and reading it back. Calling the setter on a child that does not report an interval throws NotSupportedException; a non-positive value throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException before any request is sent. The console gains a 'child <id|index> interval <seconds>' action. This release is additive: no existing public API signatures changed.",
